{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NSExpression","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSExpression","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}],"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default value of this property is an expression that evaluates to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Set this property to "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to reset it to the default value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can set this property to an expression containing any of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Constant ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethod","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Any of the following constant string values:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": The legacy hillshade method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"basic","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Basic hillshade. Uses a simple physics model where the reflected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"light intensity is proportional to the cosine of the angle between the incident"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"light and the surface normal. Similar to GDAL’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"type":"text","text":" default algorithm."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade algorithm whose intensity scales with slope. Similar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to GDAL’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"-combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" option."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm which tries to minimize effects on other map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"features beneath. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"multidirectional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade with multiple illumination directions. Uses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the basic hillshade model with multiple independent light sources."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Predefined functions, including mathematical and string operators"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Conditional expressions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Variable assignments and references to assigned variables"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Step functions applied to the "},{"code":"$zoomLevel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" variable"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This property does not support applying interpolation functions to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$zoomLevel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" variable or applying interpolation or step functions to feature","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attributes.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The hillshade algorithm to use, one of ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethodStandard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethodBasic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodCombined"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodIgor"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNHillshadeMethodMultidirectional"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer\/hillshadeMethod"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnhillshadestylelayer\/hillshademethod"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"hillshadeMethod","fragments":[{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNHillshadeStyleLayer(py)hillshadeMethod","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a style layer that renders raster "},{"type":"text","text":"digital elevation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"model"},{"type":"text","text":" (DEM) tiles on the map."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","title":"MLNHillshadeStyleLayer","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNHillshadeStyleLayer"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnhillshadestylelayer","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/Ma